WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.452
Exercise 5: implement the SKU Sales data product.

2
00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:12.046
Where we start: the contract exists, the view does not. Tests are red.

3
00:00:12.096 --> 00:00:15.203
The contract is the specification: one view, four columns, exact types.

4
00:00:15.254 --> 00:00:21.206
Dimensions group the data, measures are aggregated. transformLogic says how.

5
00:00:21.257 --> 00:00:27.464
Option 1: let an AI coding agent do it. The contracts tell it exactly what to build.

6
00:00:27.514 --> 00:00:33.465
The tests give the agent a feedback loop to verify its own work.

7
00:00:33.515 --> 00:00:49.257
Option 2: write the view by hand. Group by SKU and year.

8
00:00:49.307 --> 00:00:55.258
Cast to int and bigint: the types are part of your contract.

9
00:00:55.308 --> 00:01:00.786
Apply the SQL file to the database.

10
00:01:00.836 --> 00:01:10.337
Run the tests again: green. The implementation fulfills the contract.

11
00:01:10.387 --> 00:01:23.050
Check the verified statement from the context: the top three SKUs of 2024.

12
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:30.182
Back in the editor: the context tells agents how to query the product.

13
00:01:30.232 --> 00:01:36.086
And the same tests are one click away.

14
00:01:36.136 --> 00:01:40.589
All checks of the view pass: types, uniqueness, and plausibility.

15
00:01:40.639 --> 00:01:50.457
Set contract and data product to active, and lint both. Done.

16
00:01:50.507 --> 00:01:54.457
Your data product is live. Next: consumer-driven contracts.
